  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Iudex">Iudex</ref> 15.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">Hyt ys awriten: ‘Ne onfoh ðu nænigne had on dome; né ne ara ðú for nanum, þæt þu þæt riht ne deme’.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-q">Scriptum est: Non attendas personam hominis in indicio, nec pro aliquo facies, ut a nero denies et iniuste iudices!</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-g-a">It is written: “Don’t look (over-)favourably upon any individual, nor give honour to any (in such a way) that justice is not served.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Es steht geschrieben: ‘Nicht begünstige du irgend eine Person im Urtheilspruch und um Keines willen schone unterlassend, den richtigen Spruch zu ertheilen’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It is written: ‘Do not favour any person in judgment, and for no one's sake be lenient so as to fail to give the right judgment’.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Deuteronomy 16:19 (cf. Exodus 23:2–3)</note>
      </div>
    </body>
